# UI verification

When you change UI, layout, styling, routing, client state, or rendered data:

Do

- Exercise the flow in the browser (click, type, submit, navigate). Appearance-only screenshots are not enough.
- Check other pages that share the state or components you touched.
- Check empty, loading, and error states; desktop and mobile if layout changed.

Don’t

- Declare UI work done from code review or a single screenshot alone.
- If the browser is unavailable, use the closest substitute (tests, curl, render script) and say what you could not verify.
